3. FEES

The Software includes a platform fee that is applied to trades it executes, at
the rates published in the documentation at the time of use. That fee forms
part of the consideration for this licence, and your use of the Software is
your agreement to it. Fee rates may change in later versions; the rates that
apply are those documented for the version you are running.

The fee instruction is part of the same on chain transaction as the trade, so a
trade that does not land is not charged. Fees that are charged are taken on
chain at the time of the trade and are not refundable.

The platform fee is separate from, and in addition to, fees charged by third
parties, including pump.fun, the Solana network, priority fees, Jito tips and
account rent. Those are not received by the licensor.


4. CONFIGURATION, UPDATES AND TELEMETRY

The Software contacts a server operated by the licensor from time to time, to
retrieve its configuration and to check whether a newer version is available.
No other host is contacted for that purpose.

That check in also transmits a small set of anonymous usage counters and crash
indicators, as described in the documentation. By running the Software you
consent to this. There is no opt out in the current version.

The Software does not transmit wallet addresses, private keys, recovery
phrases, passphrases, coin addresses, trade details, amounts, RPC endpoints,
API keys or file paths.

When you accept an available update, the Software downloads and installs a new
version of itself and restarts. It does not replace itself without your action.


5. YOUR KEYS AND YOUR FUNDS ARE YOURS ALONE

The Software generates and stores cryptographic keys on your own machine. The
licensor has no access to them and cannot recover, reset, restore or replace
any recovery phrase, private key or passphrase, and cannot recover any funds.
Loss of your recovery phrase or passphrase means permanent, irreversible loss
of access to the associated wallets and everything in them. Keeping a secure
backup is entirely your responsibility.


6. TRADING RISK AND NO ADVICE

The Software places real financial transactions on a public blockchain, using
your funds, automatically and without further confirmation once configured.
Those transactions are irreversible.

Nothing produced by the Software or its documentation is financial, investment,
tax or legal advice. Every trade the Software makes is one you configured and
initiated. You are solely responsible for your trading decisions, for the
tokens you create or buy, and for any losses.

You are responsible for ensuring that your use of the Software is lawful where
you are, including any securities, tax, anti-fraud, anti-money-laundering and
market-conduct obligations that apply to you. You must not use the Software to
defraud, deceive or manipulate other market participants, or for any unlawful
